[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Public response admission and measurement lookup boundaries

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RESPONSE-MATRIX-ADMISSION-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bound matrix dimensions independently of storage shape
STATEMENT: >>>
Matrix admission shall accept dimensions1and256with matching finite storage and
RHS shape, and reject dimension0or257even when their storage and RHS shapes
match. Malformed storage/RHS lengths shall independently return InvalidInput.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: matrix_dimension_limits_and_malformed_shapes_are_independent.
Zero-valued admitted matrices are not claimed solvable; this is validation only.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RESPONSE-COMPLEX-FINITE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Reject either nonfinite complex response component
STATEMENT: >>>
The public complex compatibility solve shall reject a nonfinite real or
imaginary response component independently, and reject incorrect response
lengths, with NumericalFailure instead of publishing malformed data.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: complex_response_components_and_shape_are_validated_independently
uses deliberately invalid scripted responses and one-call accounting. Actual
DenseLu solves the scalar complex identity for the positive numerical control.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LOOKUP-AXIS-KNOT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve typed failures and exact-knot precedence
STATEMENT: >>>
Measurement lookup shall reject empty, malformed or out-of-range data/queries
with InvalidInput and a nonempty reason. Exact sample times shall return their
recorded values before interpolation; valid interior queries shall interpolate
only within the recorded axis.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: measurement_empty_malformed_and_outside_queries_stay_typed_failures
and exact_measurement_knots_precede_strict_interior_interpolation. The linear
2t+1fixture includes adjacent representable times around an interior knot.
No exact diagnostic-text contract is introduced; range-reason mutation remains
an explicitly open diagnostic question rather than a claimed numerical defect.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EXPR-UNARY-BOUNDARY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve unary slopes and recursion admission
STATEMENT: >>>
Selected inverse-sine/cosine values and slopes shall agree with circle geometry
within the tested1e-13absolute bounds. Direct inverse/log evaluation shall admit
the depth64fixtures and reject deeper counterparts without relying on unrelated
domain or overflow failures. Absolute value shall preserve its existing sign
slope, including the explicit zero-slope cusp convention, and the same depth bound.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: inverse_trigonometric_slopes_match_circle_geometry uses the3-4-5
triangle and64generated dyadic inputs[-0.875,0.875], Proptest seed2026111933.
inverse_and_log_recursion_guards_are_not_masked_by_domain_errors uses Asin(0)
chains and Log(Exp(0)) pairs, with valid controls before the deeper negatives.
absolute_value_preserves_the_sign_convention_and_recursion_bound adds positive,
negative and zero controls plus its independent depth64/65case.
This does not prove arbitrary expression accuracy or domain coverage.
<<<
